{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe heat in Paris is oppressive, though the air is thick with the scent of frying onions from the street stalls. This morning we moved out of the Hôtel des Princes, leaving our baggage at Cousin’s, a man of great intellect but little practical sense. We spent the hours hunting for a *chambre garnie*, a task more tedious than deciphering the *Geist*. Finally, at 11, we settled for a modest room near the Seine. Cousin insisted on a brief breakfast: cutlets, decent but heavy, and a bottle of good Burgundy. He is frantic to get my letter to the post by two, fearing the mail coaches have already departed.\n\nI am tired. The dust here is worse than in the Rhineland. Tell the boys to mind their conduct; I expect them to be orderly, not merely happy.\n\nYour husband,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795219225,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":191,"prompt_tokens":1121,"total_tokens":1312,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-q1FpcgS6Zg4f99ANQyuhK9PVvj2NKBpl","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1121,"prompt_ms":1111.027,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9911034790365745,"prompt_per_second":1008.976379511929,"predicted_n":191,"predicted_ms":4470.973,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.53143684210526,"predicted_per_second":42.49634251873138}}